codex
Both sensitivity gates behaved correctly: mutating the embedded executed body changed the concrete result to `(1,1)` and made the claim stick; mutating only the expected result to false `(2,5)` parsed successfully and stuck at the true `(2,11/5)`. The six submitted claims are therefore non-vacuous and genuinely body-dependent. The remaining defect is adequacy, not fake closure: they prove only finitely fixed sizes/cases plus arbitrary values at length two.
